  "report_period": "Week 6 (30th Jan to 6th Feb 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Tsakos Shipping & Trading committed the Capesize \"Irene II\" 180/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 21 mill. Note that a couple of months ago, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Montecristo\" 180/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS 06/2028, DD 06/2026, Scrubber fitted) was sold at low USD 20 mill. Furthermore, the \"Robusto\" 174/2006 SWS, China (SS/DD 09/2026, Scrubber fitted) of TMS Dry was committed to Chinese interests at USD 19,5 mill basis delivery Q2 2026, while the sister vessel \"Pompano\" 174/2006 SWS, China (SS/DD 06/2026, Scrubber fitted) from the same owners, was committed in December at high USD 17 mill basis delivery May'26. The Kamsarmax \"Athina Carras\" 82/2012 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) from Carras Hellas was committed to Greek interests at USD 17,5 mill. Remind you that back in October, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Montana I\" 82/2011 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 12/2025) was sold at USD 15,4 mill. In addition, Ciner Ship Management committed the \"Rize\" 82/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) to Greek interests at USD 17,6 mill. On the Ultramax sector, MPP Carriers committed the \"Mitsos\" 63/2013 Chengxi, China (SS 06/2028, DD 09/2026) to Greek interests at USD 20,5 mill. For reference, the two-years-younger \"Beauty Jasmine\" 63/2015 CSI, China (SS 04/2030, DD 03/2028) was sold back in November at USD 23 mill. The Handysize \"Darya Tapti\" 36/2015 Shikoku, Japan (SS 01/2030, DD 04/2028) of Chellaram Shipping was committed to clients of MGJ at USD 18,4 mill. Remind you that back in November, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Atlantic Bulker\" 36/2014 Shikoku, Japan (SS/DD 03/2027) was sold at USD 15 mill.",
    "tankers": "Following the sales of the VLCC \"DHT China\" & \"DHT Europe\" 317/2007 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 05/2027 & SS/DD 04/2027, Scrubber fitted) a month ago at USD 50,8 mill each, DHT Holdings have now committed the \"DHT Bauhinia\" 301/2007 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 01/2027, Scrubber fitted) at USD 51,5 mill. Moreover, the \"Asian Lion\" 207/2009 Shanghai, China (SS 05/2029, DD 07/2027, Scrubber fitted) was committed to Greek interests at USD 60 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Advantage Value\" 297/2009 Shanghai, China (SS 01/2029, DD 12/2026) was sold to Sinokor at USD 55 mill. The MR2 \"Seaways Grace\" & \"Seaways Madeleine\" 50/2008 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 02/2028, DD 04/2026 & SS 07/2028, DD 08/2026) were committed at high USD 16 mill each. Remind you that back in December, the sisters \"Seaways Olive\" & \"Seaways Star\" 50/2008 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 08/2028, DD 09/2026 & SS 03/2028, DD 03/2026) were committed at USD 16 mill each.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid/high usd 8,00's fio range.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/15,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 8,000/10,000 pd range. Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/16,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were fixed around usd 22,000/23,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the us 400K/500K. East Coast South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/700K.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Trips from North China into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. West Coast Indian coastal trips were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 140K/160K. West African trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 19,000/21,00000 pd. East Coast South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K/600K.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "South East Asia trips via Australia into Japan were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd. Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 7,000/8,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into Australia were fixed around usd 6,000/7,000 pd. Continental trips into West Arica were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Baltic into West Coast Central America were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Continent-Mediterranean range were reported at the level of usd 14,000/17,000 pd."
    }
  },
